 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T12:59+08:00",
 "answer": "**Probably okay for a short, easy ride if the air stays as it is now—but check again before you go.** The latest Kuching reading I found is **API 65 (moderate), recorded this morning, October 17**; that’s below the level where Malaysia’s Health Ministry advises avoiding strenuous outdoor activity (API above 100). ([jerebumalaysia.com](https://jerebumalaysia.com/en/stations/kuching-sarawak/?utm_source=openai))\n\nBecause that reading is from the morning, it may not reflect this evening. Check the official APIMS/NREB reading close to departure; if it’s **over 100**, or the haze looks noticeably worse, skip the ride. Be more cautious if you have asthma or heart/lung disease, or if you’re unusually sensitive to haze. ([eqms.doe.gov.my](https://eqms.doe.gov.my/apims/main?utm_source=openai))\n\nAlso, thunderstorms are forecast this evening, so postpone if lightning or heavy rain develops. ",
